xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium
  * Undo the flow-cache probe on cached output drops (#15947
    H29-04 arm 2): a completing ACK dropped by the cached
    output-filter or policer verdicts had already charged the
    session and promoted both handshake halves locally, with its
    HA Update merely withheld. The drop arm now rolls the probe
    back — un-charge, discard the withheld Update, restore the
    pending handshake — so a dropped packet leaves no session
    effect; a retransmitted ACK completes and publishes normally.

