xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium
  * Fix NAT allocator/scope defects (#15948): restore displaced
    non-persistent reservations after sole-holder rollback, count
    merged idle-lease grants and refuse contended merges, keep active
    deterministic NAT64 BIBs out of the idle-expiry index, judge
    fabric NAT64 sessions by geometry, thread NAT scope into
    MissingNeighbor seeds, clamp NAT64 TCP MSS, probe the NAT64
    egress hop on MissingNeighbor drops, and treat reject as terminal
    in recursive static expansion.

  * Fix compiler/show parity defects (#15944): per-family
    primary/preferred compilation is now order-independent (an
    inet6-first unit no longer leaks its IPv6 primary/preferred into
    IPv4 consumers) and a not-yet-installed primary promotes over an
    incumbent subnet peer; logical-only RETH units and IRB/fabric
    networkd models carry their configured MTU and primary/preferred;
    depth-1 packed screen families (e.g. `tcp syn-flood
    alarm-threshold 100 attack-threshold 500;`) compile every option;
    `system backup-router` destinations accumulate across nodes and
    the remote show renders all of them with a family-aware default;
    remote `show system license` uses the shared LicenseText RPC;
    repeated `netconf` siblings set NetconfSSH; and cluster
    heartbeat/sync/VRF/duplicate-identity lookups resolve authored
    Junos interface names to kernel ifnames; family-unspecified
    (hostname) syslog collectors again resolve an IPv6-only unit's
    primary. The userspace-MTU on-wire arm of H4-04 remains
    NEEDS_VALIDATION: the Go snapshot value reaches the Rust
    validator and its per-ifindex egress merge (validated, shared,
    or zero-filled), but no live oversized-frame/PTB measurement was
    run, so no wire consequence is claimed fixed.

